From 28d3176810c1f5b6188c91427127ccd3cdb8b974 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:36:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Stadium transformations: their own bit in
 arithmetic_flags, slippi_patches as in the base

Bit 1 of slippi_patches already means MSL_PATCH_PREVENT_WOBBLING to drivers
on newer layouts (tools/replay/replay_drive.py writes bits 1 to 6 from the
replay's codes), so nearly every replay turned transformations on, and bits
2 to 7 were refused. slippi_patches is the base's again: only bit 0 is read,
nothing is refused. The setting is MSL_CONFIG_STADIUM_TRANSFORMATIONS, bit 7
of arithmetic_flags, the one byte whose other bits every driver leaves clear
(the core has always refused them).

The Stadium checks are one function, msl_core_stadium_config_error, which
match construction runs. stadium-defaults-smoke (no game data) runs it on
the replay driver's config (config_from_tape, every slippi_patches value and
each arithmetic mode), the validation runner's (over the wire) and the
API's (over noise), on every legal stage, against default GameData. It
fails on the old bit ("replay_drive: transformations on (stage 2, value
0x02)") and passes now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
